{"name":"Daerlun","status":"ok","title":"Daerlun","pageId":23150,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Daerlun</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography<sup id=\"cite_ref-S.M_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.M-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">City</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sembia\" title=\"Sembia\">Sembia </a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Interior_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Interior Faerûn\">interior Faerûn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Metropolis</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-73_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-73-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-83_5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-83-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"demonym\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Demonym</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Daerlunian<sup id=\"cite_ref-WotW_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-WotW-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><table class=\"percentagetable\"><tbody><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Human</a>  </td><td> 96%  </td></tr><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Halfling\" title=\"Halfling\">Halfling</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Half-elf\" title=\"Half-elf\">Half-elf</a>, other  </td><td> 4%  </td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"religion\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Religions</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Primarily <a href=\"/wiki/Sune\" title=\"Sune\">Sune</a>; <a href=\"/wiki/Tyr\" title=\"Tyr\">Tyr</a> as a<br>facade</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Commerce<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-AWRC-p75_6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-AWRC-p75-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-C-p25_7-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-C-p25-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"imports\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Imports</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Parchment\" title=\"Parchment\">Parchment</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Wine\" title=\"Wine\">wine</a>, wool</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"exports\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Exports</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Livestock, <a href=\"/wiki/Linen\" title=\"Linen\">linens</a>, textiles</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Politics<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-GTotR-60_8-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GTotR-60-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"rulertype\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Ruler type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">High Bergun</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-GTotR-60_8-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GTotR-60-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-CotD-p33_9-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CotD-p33-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p189_10-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p189-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p176_11-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p176-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">44,000&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1358_DR\" title=\"1358 DR\">1358&#160;DR</a><br>52,477&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372&#160;DR</a><br>40,000&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479&#160;DR</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"ruler1\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">High Bergun</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"Halath Tymmyr (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGFsYXRoX1R5bW15cj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Halath Tymmyr</span>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1358_DR\" title=\"1358 DR\">1358&#160;DR</a><br>Halath Tymmyr&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367&#160;DR</a><br>Halath Tymmyr&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1370_DR\" title=\"1370 DR\">1370&#160;DR</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Daerlun\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Daerlun\">Inhabitants of  Daerlun</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Daerlun\" title=\"Category:Locations in Daerlun\">Locations in  Daerlun</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Daerlun\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Daerlun\">Organizations in  Daerlun</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"DPL-purge plainlinks\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Template:Category_intersection_jump?DPL_cat1=Locations_in__Daerlun&DPL_cat2=Roads&action=purge\">Roads  in  Daerlun</a></span></nav>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Daerlun</b> was a large city in <a href=\"/wiki/Sembia\" title=\"Sembia\">Sembia</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p176_11-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p176-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Government\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Government</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Defenses\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Defenses</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Trade\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trade</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Notable_Inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Inhabitants</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Notes\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notes</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Gallery\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Gallery</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Government\">Government</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Government\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Government\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As of <a href=\"/wiki/1368_DR\" title=\"1368 DR\">1368&#160;DR</a>, the city was run by an elderly merchant named <span class=\"new\" title=\"Halath Tymmyr (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGFsYXRoX1R5bW15cj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Halath Tymmyr</span>, although he was a puppet for the evil commander of the guard, <a href=\"/wiki/Allathast\" title=\"Allathast\">Allathast</a>, who was a member of the <a href=\"/wiki/Cult_of_the_Dragon\" title=\"Cult of the Dragon\">Cult of the Dragon</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-CotD-p33_9-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CotD-p33-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p><i>Circa</i> <a href=\"/wiki/1380_DR\" title=\"1380 DR\">1380&#160;DR</a>, Daerlun came under the control of the <a href=\"/wiki/Netherese_Empire\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Netherese Empire\">Netherese Empire</a> along with the rest of Sembia,<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p176_11-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p176-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> but was annexed by <a href=\"/wiki/Cormyr\" title=\"Cormyr\">Cormyr</a> in the <a href=\"/wiki/1397_DR\" title=\"1397 DR\">Year of the Quill, 1397 DR</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Dun198.CR-p61_12-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Dun198.CR-p61-12\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The city declared itself a neutral independent city-state in the <a href=\"/wiki/1439_DR\" title=\"1439 DR\">Year of the Silent Tear, 1439 DR</a>, rather than be absorbed by Cormyr or stay under the direct influence of Sembia.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p176_11-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p176-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Defenses\">Defenses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Defenses\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Defenses\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Daerlun was the most heavily fortified city in Sembia, and boasted the tallest curtain wall on all of <a href=\"/wiki/Toril\" title=\"Toril\">Toril</a>. This 500‑foot-tall (150‑meter) wall was made of <a href=\"/wiki/Magic\" title=\"Magic\">magically</a> hard <a href=\"/wiki/Obsidian\" title=\"Obsidian\">obsidian</a> and was erected by the Netherese Empire in the <a href=\"/wiki/1382_DR\" title=\"1382 DR\">Year of the Black Blazon, 1382 DR</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p176_11-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p176-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-13\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>note 1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> It was garrisoned by a massive army of conscripts from across Sembia, who drilled on massive parade grounds near the city's markets.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p176_11-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p176-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> \n</p><p>Patrols out of Daerlun—mounted on flying <a href=\"/wiki/Griffon\" title=\"Griffon\">griffons</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/Veserab\" title=\"Veserab\">veserabs</a>—ranged as far as the <a href=\"/wiki/Vast_Swamp\" title=\"Vast Swamp\">Vast Swamp</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/Thunder_Peaks\" title=\"Thunder Peaks\">Thunder Peaks</a>, and the southern <a href=\"/wiki/Dales\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dales\">Dales</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p176_11-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p176-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trade\">Trade</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Trade\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Trade\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The city had a bustling marketplace and a wealthy trade quarter.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p176_11-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p176-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>As of the mid-14<sup>th</sup> century <a href=\"/wiki/DR\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>, Daerlunian linen sold for around 8 <a href=\"/wiki/Sp\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Sp\">sp</a> per square yard, while Daerlunian wool sold for between 9 sp and 2 <a href=\"/wiki/Gp\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Gp\">gp</a> per square yard depending on the weight of the fabric.<sup id=\"cite_ref-AWRC-p75_6-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-AWRC-p75-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The city imported such commodities as <a href=\"/wiki/Parchment\" title=\"Parchment\">parchment</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Wine\" title=\"Wine\">wine</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Wool\" title=\"Wool\">wool</a> from <a href=\"/wiki/Eveningstar\" title=\"Eveningstar\">Eveningstar</a> in Cormyr.<sup id=\"cite_ref-C-p25_7-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-C-p25-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The evil semi-religious organization, the Cult of the Dragon, had a presence in Daerlun as of the mid-to-late 14<sup>th</sup> century DR, but preferred a secretive approach, using the city as a place to store armaments and to treat wounded members. The commander of the city guard, Allathast, used the elderly merchant Halath Tymmyr as a puppet to rule the city.<sup id=\"cite_ref-CotD-p33_9-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CotD-p33-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In the <a href=\"/wiki/1484_DR\" title=\"1484 DR\">Year of the Awakened Sleepers, 1484 DR</a>, the city prepared defenses against a possible <a href=\"/wiki/Shadovar\" title=\"Shadovar\">Shadovar</a> and Sembian invasion. Rumors abounded in the city about gods, war, and natural disasters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-The_Godborn-385_14-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-The_Godborn-385-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=5\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n\n\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Alask%27s_Arrow\" title=\"Alask's Arrow\">Alask's Arrow</a>: Decent inn and tavern.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Bergun_Hall\" title=\"Bergun Hall\">Bergun Hall</a>: Courthouse and records library.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-83_5-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-83-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-D287-70_15-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D287-70-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/Black_Banner_Inn\" title=\"Black Banner Inn\">Black Banner Inn</a>: High-class accommodations with gambling and a well-stocked wine cellar on the <a href=\"/wiki/Street_of_the_Dragon\" title=\"Street of the Dragon\">Street of the Dragon</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-D287-70_15-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D287-70-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Firehair\" title=\"House of Firehair\">House of Firehair</a>: Large walled temple complex in the center of town.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/Mighty_Mace\" title=\"Mighty Mace\">Mighty Mace</a>: Another fine inn and tavern that faced the Westmarket.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-D287-70_15-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D287-70-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Oakwaters\" title=\"Oakwaters\">Oakwaters</a>: The city's large public bathing pool.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-83_5-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-83-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/Old_Plough\" title=\"Old Plough\">Old Plough</a>: Not-so-fine inn and tavern.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>Place of Banners: Large, open area in the center of the city that contained Bergun Hall.<sup id=\"cite_ref-D287-70_15-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D287-70-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>The Sea Arch: The southern gate into the city; opened onto <a href=\"/wiki/Barrel_Lane\" title=\"Barrel Lane\">Barrel Lane</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-D287-70_15-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D287-70-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Shadowdark_House\" title=\"Shadowdark House\">Shadowdark House</a>: A magic shop on <a href=\"/wiki/Saurovin_Street\" title=\"Saurovin Street\">Saurovin Street</a>.</li>\n<li>The Sunset Gate: The western gate into the city.<sup id=\"cite_ref-D287-70_15-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D287-70-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/Westmarket\" title=\"Westmarket\">Westmarket</a>: Large, open marketplace on the west side.<sup id=\"cite_ref-D287-70_15-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D287-70-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Inhabitants\">Notable Inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notable Inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=6\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Aerbront\" title=\"Aerbront\">Aerbront</a>: A kind <a href=\"/wiki/Wizard\" title=\"Wizard\">wizard</a>, sharper than he pretended to be.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Alask (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQWxhc2s/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Alask \"Eagle-eyes\"</span>: Owner/operator of Alask's Arrow inn and tavern.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-9\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Dhelarr (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRGhlbGFycj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Dhelarr \"the Night Blade\"</span>: Paymaster of the <a href=\"/wiki/Firehands_Group\" title=\"Firehands Group\">Firehands Group</a> trading coster.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-10\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Elmareen_Whistestone\" title=\"Elmareen Whistestone\">Elmareen Whistestone</a>: Magical researcher, tutor, and reputed dragonslayer.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-11\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Halath Tymmyr (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGFsYXRoX1R5bW15cj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Halath Tymmyr</span>: Old merchant. High Bergun in name only.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-12\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-GTotR-60_8-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GTotR-60-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-CotD-p33_9-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CotD-p33-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Harlyn_Grimmerhand\" title=\"Harlyn Grimmerhand\">Harlyn Grimmerhand</a>: Retired <a href=\"/wiki/Warrior\" title=\"Warrior\">warrior</a>, tutor, horse breeder, investor.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-13\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Minthalar\" title=\"Minthalar\">Minthalar \"the Many-eyed\"</a>: Well-informed merchant that could get most anything for a price.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-14\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Othnyl_Risingstone\" title=\"Othnyl Risingstone\">Othnyl Risingstone</a>: Premier stone cutter, sculptor, and part-time weapons smith.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-15\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Sandar_Kathklan\" title=\"Sandar Kathklan\">Sandar \"Silkenvoice\" Kathklan</a>: Potion- and poison-maker, <a href=\"/wiki/Necromancer\" title=\"Necromancer\">necromancer</a>, dangerous.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-16\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Tarbrost_Mathos\" title=\"Tarbrost Mathos\">Tarbrost \"The Bull\" Mathos</a>: tutor and quartermaster of the city guard.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-82_4-17\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-82-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Thauna_Maskalar\" title=\"Thauna Maskalar\">Thauna Maskalar</a>: High Priestess of the House of Firehair.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Thelbaerone_Shadowdark\" title=\"Thelbaerone Shadowdark\">Thelbaerone Shadowdark</a>: Wizard, sage, and proprietress of <a href=\"/wiki/Shadowdark_House\" title=\"Shadowdark House\">Shadowdark House</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=7\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"metadata plainlinks stub\"><tbody><tr>\n<td><i>This article is incomplete.</i>  <i>You can help the Forgotten Realms Wiki by providing more information.</i></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notes\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=8\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notes\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<small><div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-13\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-13\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Canon\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Canon\">Canon</a> material does not provide an exact date for when the Netherese raised Daerlun's wall, but <a href=\"/wiki/Brian_R._James\" title=\"Brian R. James\">Brian R. James</a>, one of the authors of the <i><a href=\"/wiki/Forgotten_Realms_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide\">Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide</a></i> in which the wall is discussed, clarified in a <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://archive.today/2024.10.31-023313/https://x.com/brianrjames/status/1621036856\">Tweet</a> that it was built in 1382 DR.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></small>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Gallery\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=9\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Gallery\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"18be20321dde8f575ec0559b5d250878\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"lightbox-caption\" style=\"width:185px;\"><i>The city of Daerlun circa <a href=\"/wiki/1358_DR\" title=\"1358 DR\">1358 DR</a>.</i></div></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"lightbox-caption\" style=\"width:185px;\"><i>2nd edition map showing Daerlun c. <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367 DR</a>.</i></div></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"lightbox-caption\" style=\"width:185px;\"><i>3rd edition map showing Daerlun c. <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a>.</i></div></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"lightbox-caption\" style=\"width:185px;\"><i>4th edition map showing Daerlun c. <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479 DR</a>.</i></div></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"lightbox-caption\" style=\"width:185px;\"><i>A map of Daerlun from the Interactive Atlas.</i></div></div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Daerlun?veaction=edit&section=10\" aria-label=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-S.M-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-S.M_1-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Map included in&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Paul_S._Kemp\" title=\"Paul S. Kemp\">Paul S. Kemp</a>&#160;(December 2008). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Shadowrealm\" title=\"Shadowrealm\">Shadowrealm</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>). ISBN&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0786948639\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0786948639\">978-0786948639</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-WotW-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-WotW_2-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ed_Greenwood\" title=\"Ed Greenwood\">Ed Greenwood</a>&#160;(August 1992). “<a href=\"/wiki/The_Everwinking_Eye\" title=\"The Everwinking Eye\">The Everwinking Eye</a>: Words To The Wise”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Jean_Rabe\" title=\"Jean Rabe\">Jean Rabe</a>&#160;ed. <a href=\"/wiki/Polyhedron_74\" title=\"Polyhedron 74\"><i>Polyhedron</i> #74</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 14–15.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRA-73-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRA-73_3-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Jeff_Grubb\" title=\"Jeff Grubb\">Jeff Grubb</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Ed_Greenwood\" title=\"Ed Greenwood\">Ed Greenwood</a>&#160;(1990). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Forgotten_Realms_Adventures\" title=\"Forgotten Realms Adventures\">Forgotten Realms Adventures</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"TSR, Inc\">TSR, Inc</a